  "worked_solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{\u2032}(t)}{{x}^{\u2032}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,{y}^{\u2032}(t)=\\frac{9}{2}\\sqrt{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{(\\frac{9}{2}\\sqrt{t})}{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}=9t.\n$$",
